    "code": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nvoid dfs(int r, int c, int grid[100][100], int i, int j, int oldColor, int newColor) {\n    if (i < 0 || i >= r || j < 0 || j >= c || grid[i][j] != oldColor) return;\n    grid[i][j] = newColor;\n    dfs(r, c, grid, i + 1, j, oldColor, newColor);\n    dfs(r, c, grid, i - 1, j, oldColor, newColor);\n    dfs(r, c, grid, i, j + 1, oldColor, newColor);\n    dfs(r, c, grid, i, j - 1, oldColor, newColor);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int r, c, sr, sc, newColor;\n    if (scanf(\"%d %d %d %d %d\", &r, &c, &sr, &sc, &newColor) == 5) {\n        int grid[100][100];\n        for (int i = 0; i < r; i++) for (int j = 0; j < c; j++) scanf(\"%d\", &grid[i][j]);\n        int oldColor = grid[sr][sc];\n        if (oldColor != newColor) dfs(r, c, grid, sr, sc, oldColor, newColor);\n        for (int i = 0; i < r; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < c; j++) {\n                printf(\"%d%s\", grid[i][j], (j == c - 1) ? \"\" : \" \");\n            }\n            printf(\"\\n\");\n        }\n    }\n    return 0;\n}",
    "explanation": "1. Read matrix input.\n2. Apply 2D grid processing algorithm for Flood Fill Algorithm.\n3. Print result.\n\nTime Complexity: O(N * M)\nSpace Complexity: O(N * M)",
    "timeComplexity": "O(N * M)",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(N * M)"
