    "scenario": "Practical C problem covering Searching & Sorting for Medium level placement preparation.",
    "code": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n\ntypedef struct { int start; int end; } Interval;\nint compare(const void *a, const void *b) {\n    return ((Interval*)a)->start - ((Interval*)b)->start;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    if (scanf(\"%d\", &n) == 1 && n > 0) {\n        Interval intervals[100];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) scanf(\"%d %d\", &intervals[i].start, &intervals[i].end);\n        qsort(intervals, n, sizeof(Interval), compare);\n        Interval merged[100];\n        int m = 0;\n        merged[0] = intervals[0];\n        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {\n            if (intervals[i].start <= merged[m].end) {\n                if (intervals[i].end > merged[m].end) merged[m].end = intervals[i].end;\n            } else {\n                m++;\n                merged[m] = intervals[i];\n            }\n        }\n        for (int i = 0; i <= m; i++) printf(\"%d %d\\n\", merged[i].start, merged[i].end);\n    }\n    return 0;\n}",
    "explanation": "1. Read input sequence.\n2. Apply search/sort algorithm for Merge Overlapping Intervals.\n3. Output result.\n\nTime Complexity: O(N log N)\nSpace Complexity: O(N)",
