    "difficulty": "Easy",
    "category": "Basic Numbers",
    "problemStatement": "[JAVA] Given a positive integer N, check whether N is an Armstrong number. An n-digit number is an Armstrong number if the sum of its digits raised to the power n equals the number itself.",
    "inputDesc": "A single positive integer N.",
    "outputDesc": "Print 'Armstrong' if N is Armstrong, else print 'Not Armstrong'.",
    "constraints": "1 <= N <= 10^9",
    "exampleInput": "153",
    "exampleOutput": "Armstrong",
    "scenario": "Practical JAVA problem covering Basic Numbers for Easy level placement preparation.",
    "code": "import java.util.Scanner;\npublic class Solution {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        if (sc.hasNextLong()) {\n            long n = sc.nextLong();\n            String s = String.valueOf(n);\n            int digits = s.length();\n            long temp = n, sum = 0;\n            while (temp > 0) {\n                long d = temp % 10;\n                long p = 1;\n                for(int i=0; i<digits; i++) p *= d;\n                sum += p;\n                temp /= 10;\n            }\n            if (sum == n) System.out.println(\"Armstrong\");\n            else System.out.println(\"Not Armstrong\");\n        }\n    }\n}",
    "explanation": "1. Count total digits d in N.\n2. Calculate sum of each digit raised to power d.\n3. If sum equals N, print 'Armstrong', else 'Not Armstrong'.\n\nTime Complexity: O(log10 N)\nSpace Complexity: O(1)",
