    "problemStatement": "[JAVA] Given an N x M matrix, reshape it to a new r x c matrix while preserving row-wise order.",
    "inputDesc": "Matrix dimensions followed by grid elements.",
    "outputDesc": "Processed matrix result.",
    "constraints": "1 <= N, M <= 500",
    "exampleInput": "2 2 1 4\n1 2\n3 4",
    "exampleOutput": "1 2 3 4",
    "scenario": "Practical JAVA problem covering Matrices for Medium level placement preparation.",
    "code": "import java.util.Scanner;\npublic class Solution {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        if (sc.hasNextInt()) {\n            int r = sc.nextInt();\n            int c = sc.nextInt();\n            int nr = sc.nextInt();\n            int nc = sc.nextInt();\n            int[][] mat = new int[r][c];\n            for (int i = 0; i < r; i++) for (int j = 0; j < c; j++) mat[i][j] = sc.nextInt();\n            if (r * c != nr * nc) {\n                for (int i = 0; i < r; i++) {\n                    for (int j = 0; j < c; j++) {\n                        System.out.print(mat[i][j] + (j == c - 1 ? \"\" : \" \"));\n                    }\n                    System.out.println();\n                }\n            } else {\n                int[] flat = new int[r * c];\n                int idx = 0;\n                for (int i = 0; i < r; i++) for (int j = 0; j < c; j++) flat[idx++] = mat[i][j];\n                idx = 0;\n                for (int i = 0; i < nr; i++) {\n                    for (int j = 0; j < nc; j++) {\n                        System.out.print(flat[idx++] + (j == nc - 1 ? \"\" : \" \"));\n                    }\n                    System.out.println();\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}",
    "explanation": "1. Read matrix input.\n2. Apply 2D grid processing algorithm for Reshape Matrix.\n3. Print result.\n\nTime Complexity: O(N * M)\nSpace Complexity: O(N * M)",
